"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/field-guide/exhibition.css\"><header class=\"topbar\">\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <a class=\"wordmark\" href=\"/\" aria-label=\"Lotolipi home\">lotolipi<span>.</span></a>\n      <nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a><a href=\"/#case-studies\">Case studies</a><a href=\"/lottolov\">Lottolov</a><a href=\"/resume\">Résumé</a><a href=\"/#contact\">Contact</a><a href=\"/lo-lab\">Lo Lab</a></nav>\n    </div>\n  </header><main id=\"main-content\"><section class=\"fg-cover\"><div><small>Visitor experience · Independent concept</small><h1>Field<br>Guide.</h1><p>A visitor has 45 minutes, two interests and a whole exhibition to explore. How much room can a route leave for discovery?</p><a href=\"/field-guide/index.html\">Plan a visit →</a></div><img src=\"/field-guide/materials.webp\" alt=\"Sculptural indigo textile and a carved printing cylinder on a vermilion plinth\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></section><section class=\"work\"><div class=\"wrap\"><header class=\"work-head\"><p class=\"label\">Independent concept · Fictional exhibition</p><h2>A route with room to change.</h2><p>I designed a single-floor exhibition with twelve exhibits across three galleries. A route starts with the visitor’s interests, time budget and access preferences.</p></header><img src=\"/field-guide/floor.svg\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:16px;margin:24px 0 40px\" alt=\"Cloth, Impression and Object galleries share a corridor\"><div class=\"walkthrough-copy\"><h3>Start with curiosity.</h3><p>Open a gallery and choose an exhibit. Each one offers a detail to look for. Choose “Start my route here” to make that object the first stop in your itinerary.</p><h3>Show where the time goes.</h3><p>Each numbered stop names its gallery, its subject, the walk to get there and the viewing time. The planner first tries to represent both interests, then fills the remaining time with up to four stops. The step-free filter excludes the raised displays.</p><h3>Make the detour a choice.</h3><p>Try the default textiles and printmaking route. Give the indigo loom ten more minutes. Before you commit, the guide names the stop you would lose. One action restores the original route.</p><h3>Asha’s step-free visit</h3><p>In a fictional scenario walkthrough, Asha has 45 minutes and wants to start with the block-print demonstration. Choosing an exhibit took her straight to a route, past the access setting. I moved the step-free choice into the exhibit view as well. Asha can now set it before starting, keep it when she takes a detour, and change it later in the planner.</p><h3>What remains to learn</h3><p>Walking and viewing times are illustrative. A visitor study would test whether people understand the trade-off before they change the route and whether the timing feels realistic on the floor.</p><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/field-guide/index.html\">Try the route planner →</a></div></div></section><section class=\"wrap social-context\"><h2>Beyond the case study.</h2><a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lotologique/\">Product logic and design findings · @lotologique ↗</a></section><section class=\"wrap social-context\"><p>Design context: connectivity differs across populations. Explore the <a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"/lo-lab\">global connectivity data experiment</a>. It is not evidence about this prototype’s users.</p></section></main><footer class=\"footer\" id=\"contact\">\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <h2>Say <em>hello.</em></h2><p>Have a product role in mind? I’d love to hear what your team is building.</p>\n      <a class=\"inline-link\" href=\"mailto:smshilpi1@gmail.com\">smshilpi1@gmail.com <svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use href=\"#f7-envelope\"></use></svg></a>\n      <p class=\"closing-label\">Find me elsewhere</p><nav class=\"social-identities\" aria-label=\"Instagram profiles\"><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lotologique/\"><span>Product logic</span><strong>@lotologique ↗</strong><small>Design findings, mini case studies and experiments.</small></a><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lottolov/\"><span>Art & illustration</span><strong>@lottolov ↗</strong><small>Visual explorations, prints and everything art.</small></a><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lotolipi/\"><span>Personal</span><strong>@lotolipi ↗</strong><small>Life beyond the work.</small></a></nav><div class=\"footer-end\">\n        <span>© 2026 Shilpi Mishra · Lotolipi</span><a href=\"/ip\">Intellectual property</a><a href=\"/privacy\">Privacy</a>\n        <a class=\"back-top\" href=\"#top\">Back to top <svg class=\"icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use href=\"#f7-arrow_up\"></use></svg></a>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </footer><style>#contact.footer{padding-block:clamp(64px,10vw,144px) 48px}#contact.footer>.wrap{text-align:center}#contact.footer h2{font-size:clamp(56px,12vw,144px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:0 0 24px}#contact.footer>.wrap>p:not(.closing-label){max-width:38ch;margin:0 auto 24px;line-height:1.6}#contact.footer .closing-label{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.08em;margin:64px 0 16px}#contact.footer .social-identities{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;background:transparent!important;padding:0!important;border:0!important;margin:0 auto 48px}#contact.footer .social-identities>a{display:flex!important;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center!important;gap:10px;padding:28px 20px!important;border:1px solid currentColor!important;border-radius:18px;text-decoration:none!important;background:transparent!important;min-width:0}#contact.footer .social-identities>a>*{text-align:center!important;text-decoration:none!important;margin:0!important}#contact.footer .social-identities strong{font-size:clamp(18px,2.5vw,28px);line-height:1.2}#contact.footer .social-identities small{font-size:14px;line-height:1.5}#contact.footer .social-identities>a:hover strong{text-decoration:underline!important}#contact.footer .footer-end{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:16px 24px;padding-top:28px;font-size:13px;text-align:center}#contact.footer .footer-end>*{font-size:13px!important}#contact.footer .footer-end>span{flex-basis:100%}#contact.footer .back-top{margin:0!important}@media(max-width:47rem){#contact.footer .social-identities{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px}#contact.footer .social-identities>a{padding:24px!important}#contact.footer .closing-label{margin-top:48px}#contact.footer .footer-end{gap:16px}#contact.footer .back-top{flex-basis:100%;justify-content:center}}\n#contact.footer .social-identities>a{border:0!important;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(255,255,255,.48),rgba(255,255,255,.12))!important;box-shadow:0 6px 24px rgba(40,25,60,.06);backdrop-filter:blur(12px)}#contact.footer .social-identities>a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid currentColor;outline-offset:4px}#contact.footer .social-identities>a:hover{background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(255,255,255,.62),rgba(255,255,255,.25))!important}</style>"